One-Way ANOVA — Components 4.1
Total Sum of Squares (SST): overall variability around the grand mean.
Between-group Sum of Squares (SSB): variability explained by differences among 
group means.
Within-group Sum of Squares (SSW): variability inside the groups.
SST = SSB + SSW.
df_between = k − 1; 
df_within = N − k;
MSB = SSB/(k−1); 
MSW = SSW/(N−k); 
F = MSB/MSW.
